---
// Is my home in a flood zone or a slide area? (#509). Only free public maps
// and official pages. Not here yet: county counts of flood events and of
// buildings at landslide risk, and a City of Morgantown floodplain contact,
// because we could not read them on a current official page.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SourceLine from '../components/SourceLine.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import Route from '../components/Route.astro';
import Milepost from '../components/Milepost.astro';
import Fact from '../components/Fact.astro';
import { factsFor } from '../lib/facts.mjs';
import { telHref } from '../lib/content.mjs';
import { fixFormUrl } from '../lib/group-requests.mjs';
export const page = { door: "living-here", topic: "weather", label: "Is my home in a flood zone or a slide area?", summary: "Check an address on the state flood and landslide maps, flood insurance basics, and when you need a floodplain permit" };
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
// Steps 1 and 2, the county office and the city form are fact records in
// content/facts/flood/ (#122), re-read 2026-11-03. Still typed here: the
// ordinance paragraph (the ordinance PDF is a scan, so it cannot be quoted
// by our tools) and the landslide step (the map page loads its text by script).
const fact = factsFor('flood');
const checked = '2026-10-30';
const nfip = [{ url: 'https://www.floodsmart.gov/get-insured/buy-a-policy', checked }];
const ordinance = [
  { url: 'https://www.monongaliacounty.gov/departments/floodplain/index.php', checked },
  { url: 'https://www.monongaliacounty.gov/departments/floodplain/history.php', checked: '2026-10-31' },
  { url: 'https://www.monongaliacounty.gov/document_center/Floodplain/Floodplain%20Fillable.pdf', checked: '2026-11-01', name: 'County floodplain application (PDF)' },
  { url: 'https://www.monongaliacounty.gov/document_center/Ordinances/Monongalia%20County%20Floodplain%20Ordinance.pdf', checked, name: 'Monongalia County Floodplain Ordinance (updated March 2019)' },
];
const landslide = [{ url: 'https://www.mapwv.gov/landslide/', checked }];
const countyPhone = '304-599-6332';
---
<Base title="Is my home in a flood zone or a slide area? Mon County, WV" description="How to check a Morgantown or Monongalia County address on the West Virginia Flood Tool, the FEMA flood map and the WV Landslide Tool, what a flood zone means for insurance, and when you need a county floodplain permit.">
  <h1>Is my home in a flood zone or a slide area?</h1>
  <p class="lede">Check before you rent, buy or build. It takes a few minutes on a public map. Flooding is not covered by most home or renters insurance. Tap a step to open it.</p>

  <Route label="Steps to check a home for flood and slide risk">
  <Milepost n={1} title="Look up the address on the flood map" id="flood" open>
  <Fact f={fact('wv-flood-tool')} about="the West Virginia Flood Tool" />
  <Fact f={fact('county-red-shaded-area')} about="the county floodplain and the flood map" />
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href="https://www.mapwv.gov/flood/"><Icon name="open" /><span>Open the WV Flood Tool</span></a>
  </div>
  <Fact f={fact('fema-map-service-center')} about="the FEMA Flood Map Service Center" />
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href="https://msc.fema.gov/portal/home"><Icon name="open" /><span>Open the FEMA flood map</span></a>
  </div>

  </Milepost>

  <Milepost n={2} title="What a flood zone means for insurance" id="insurance">
  <ul>
    <Fact tag="li" f={fact('nfip-not-covered')} about="flood insurance and regular insurance" />
    <Fact tag="li" f={fact('nfip-30-day-wait')} about="the wait for a new flood policy" />
    <Fact tag="li" f={fact('nfip-renters')} about="renters flood insurance" />
  </ul>
  <p>A home outside a high risk zone can still flood. Ask an insurance agent what a policy would cost for the address.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={nfip} about="flood insurance" />

  </Milepost>

  <Milepost n={3} title="Building, adding on or filling in a floodplain needs a permit" id="permit">
  <p>In Monongalia County, you need a <strong>floodplain permit</strong> before you build, add on, make a big repair, place a manufactured home, or fill, grade or pave land in or right next to the floodplain. The county ordinance says the work cannot start until the Floodplain Administrator issues the permit.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={ordinance} about="the county floodplain permit" />
  <Fact f={fact('county-floodplain-office')} about="the county floodplain office" />
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href={telHref(countyPhone)}><Icon name="phone" /><span>Call the county floodplain office</span></a>
    <a class="btn" href="https://www.monongaliacounty.gov/departments/floodplain/index.php"><Icon name="open" /><span>County floodplain page</span></a>
  </div>
  <Fact f={fact('morgantown-floodplain-form')} about="the Morgantown floodplain permit form" />
  <p>Other permits may apply too. See <a href={`${base}/permits/`}>Do I need a building permit?</a></p>

  </Milepost>

  <Milepost n={4} title="Check for landslide risk" id="landslide">
  <p>The <strong>WV Landslide Tool</strong> is a public state map made by state agencies with FEMA. It shows where landslides have happened and which areas are more likely to slide.</p>
  <p>The map's makers say its risk results should not be read at a scale smaller than a county, and are for planning only. For a single property, they say to ask a geotechnical (soil) engineer or a landslide expert.</p>
  <SourceLine sources={landslide} about="the WV Landslide Tool" />
  <div class="actions">
    <a class="btn" href="https://www.mapwv.gov/landslide/"><Icon name="open" /><span>Open the WV Landslide Tool</span></a>
  </div>
  </Milepost>
  </Route>

  <p>Water already coming in? See <a href={`${base}/after-a-storm/`}>Storm damage, flooding or power out?</a></p>
  <p>Storm on the way? See <a href={`${base}/weather-alerts/`}>how to get official weather alerts</a>. New here? See <a href={`${base}/moving-here/`}>start power, water, gas and trash</a>.</p>
  <p class="meta">Each part shows when we last checked its source. Maps change when FEMA updates them, so check again before you sign. We describe these maps and rules and do not decide whether a property is safe. Something out of date? <a href={fixFormUrl({ page: Astro.url.pathname })}>Tell us</a>.</p>
</Base>
